# My Aria — environment variables
#
# Copy to `.env.local` and uncomment/edit. `.env.local` is gitignored.

# ─── TULA_DATA_DIR ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Absolute path to a canonical FHIR-per-resource tree on disk.
#
#   <TULA_DATA_DIR>/
#     Patient/<id>.json
#     Observation/<id>.json
#     MedicationRequest/<id>.json
#     Appointment/<id>.json
#     ...
#
# When unset (the default), My Aria renders the synthetic fixtures in
# `lib/data/fixtures.ts` — no PHI, no disk reads, hosting-clean.
#
# When set to a valid path, My Aria reads real FHIR resources and renders
# them through the same UI. The path is read at request time, not build
# time, so the same `next build` artifact serves both modes.
#
# For a personal local instance backed by your own pull data:
#   TULA_DATA_DIR=/home/youruser/.openclaw/workspace/tula/fhir
#
# For a provisioned tenant: the `tula-provision` script sets this env var
# to the tenant's per-tenant FHIR directory. See docs/HOSTING_STRATEGY.md.

# TULA_DATA_DIR=/home/azureuser/.openclaw/workspace/tula/fhir
